WEBVTT


00:00:48.973 --> 00:00:51.066
[THUNDER RUMBLING]


00:00:51.475 --> 00:00:53.443
[WOMAN CACKLING]


00:00:53.611 --> 00:00:55.340
FRED:
Come on.


00:00:59.416 --> 00:01:01.247
Split up.


00:01:04.955 --> 00:01:07.617
SHAGGY: Hey, come on, Scoob.
SCOOBY: I'm right behind you, Shaggy.


00:01:07.791 --> 00:01:09.884
[SHAGGY SCREAMS]


00:01:10.427 --> 00:01:12.588
Change of plans.


00:01:16.433 --> 00:01:18.492
WOMAN:
Stay out.


00:01:18.669 --> 00:01:20.762
[GRUNTING]


00:01:21.739 --> 00:01:24.902
Time to unmask the person
behind this mystery.


00:01:26.443 --> 00:01:29.241
- It's you?
- What?


00:01:29.413 --> 00:01:32.280
Like, it can't be.


00:01:42.893 --> 00:01:46.021
MAN: Remember, people, just because
this is the last day of class...


00:01:46.263 --> 00:01:48.288
...doesn't mean
this test doesn't count.


00:01:52.269 --> 00:01:53.497
Huh?


00:01:57.307 --> 00:01:59.036
No.


00:02:11.522 --> 00:02:12.682
Yes.


00:02:13.924 --> 00:02:16.051
Cowabunga.


00:02:20.564 --> 00:02:22.031
- Hot dog.
- Hot dog.


00:02:23.534 --> 00:02:25.502
GIRL 1:
Let's dance.


00:02:27.571 --> 00:02:29.436
Yeah.


00:02:41.852 --> 00:02:42.944
[GIRL 2 WHISTLES]


00:02:43.587 --> 00:02:47.216
Uh, guys, what are you doing?


00:02:47.458 --> 00:02:49.722
I know you're excited
the school year's over...


00:02:49.893 --> 00:02:51.952
...but our seasonal employment
awaits.


00:02:52.162 --> 00:02:55.563
Already? Like, I didn't even have time
to get a tan.


00:02:55.733 --> 00:02:57.496
- Yeah.
- Come on.


00:03:02.539 --> 00:03:04.598
[CHEERING]


00:03:08.545 --> 00:03:11.275
Well, it sure is lucky
that Daphne's uncle...


00:03:11.482 --> 00:03:14.076
...is opening his new country club
this summer, hey, V?


00:03:14.251 --> 00:03:17.379
Indeed. Without these summer jobs,
we'd never able to pay back...


00:03:17.554 --> 00:03:20.114
...Old Man Frickert
for the damage we did to his barn.


00:03:20.691 --> 00:03:22.716
Say cheese.


00:03:22.893 --> 00:03:24.224
[GIGGLES]


00:03:24.394 --> 00:03:27.090
- What is he--?
- Oh, Scoob's got a new hobby.


00:03:27.264 --> 00:03:28.731
Scrapbooking.


00:03:28.899 --> 00:03:32.130
- What happened to gardening?
- It didn't work out.


00:03:32.302 --> 00:03:35.499
Everything he planted,
he'd just dig right up.


00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:38.407
VELMA:
Hm.


00:03:38.809 --> 00:03:42.609
Daphne said we should hit the road
right after school.


00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:44.975
Any sign of her or Fred?


00:03:45.149 --> 00:03:46.707
Uh-uh.


00:03:47.785 --> 00:03:49.047
[VELMA GASPS]


00:03:49.219 --> 00:03:51.380
- Like, huh?
VELMA: Jinkies.


00:03:51.588 --> 00:03:53.055
Ooh.


00:03:53.791 --> 00:03:55.554
Perfect.


00:03:58.328 --> 00:04:01.991
Well? I for one think we deserve
an explanation.


00:04:02.166 --> 00:04:03.895
- Yeah.
- Yes.


00:04:04.101 --> 00:04:08.765
There's always been an undeniable
chemistry between you two, but--


00:04:08.939 --> 00:04:12.636
When did the transformative reaction
finally occur?


00:04:13.677 --> 00:04:16.168
I guess it started that night
at Old Man Frickert's.


00:04:16.346 --> 00:04:18.246
Yeah. Remember, Velma?


00:04:18.415 --> 00:04:22.010
We followed the trail of the vengeful
scarecrow up into the hayloft.


00:04:22.186 --> 00:04:24.120
This is impossible.


00:04:24.288 --> 00:04:26.813
We'll never find anything in here.


00:04:27.191 --> 00:04:29.853
Yes, if I wasn't so pun averse...


00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:33.188
...I might even say it's like looking
for a needle in a haystack.


00:04:33.363 --> 00:04:34.625
[MAN ROARS]


00:04:34.798 --> 00:04:36.698
MAN:
Didn't scare you, did I?


00:04:36.934 --> 00:04:38.367
[VELMA & DAPHNE SCREAMING]


00:04:38.569 --> 00:04:40.002
Daphne.


00:04:42.673 --> 00:04:44.334
Are you okay?


00:04:45.142 --> 00:04:47.110
I am now.


00:04:48.979 --> 00:04:51.277
SHAGGY: Like, run!
- What is it, Shaggy?


00:04:51.448 --> 00:04:54.781
- This one's gonna be a real barn burner.
FRED: Shaggy.


00:04:55.352 --> 00:04:57.115
Look out!


00:04:59.656 --> 00:05:02.318
DAPHNE: And thus,
we're stuck paying for a new barn.


00:05:02.492 --> 00:05:04.653
Again, just for the record...


00:05:04.828 --> 00:05:07.388
...nowhere on those bales of hay
did it say flammable.


00:05:07.598 --> 00:05:10.158
SCOOBY: Yeah.
- Anyway, that was also the night...


00:05:10.334 --> 00:05:13.462
...that Fred and I realized
we were just meant to be.


00:05:16.874 --> 00:05:18.967
It's a lovely story.


00:05:19.142 --> 00:05:22.077
But I do feel obligated
to raise one concern.


00:05:22.246 --> 00:05:24.407
Whenever there's a shift
in a relationship...


00:05:24.615 --> 00:05:27.311
...between two individuals
within a group...


00:05:27.484 --> 00:05:31.181
...it inevitably has repercussions
on the group as a whole.


00:05:32.489 --> 00:05:35.322
SHAGGY:
Oh, Velma, don't worry about that.


00:05:35.492 --> 00:05:38.325
We're all way too mature
to let that happen.


00:05:38.495 --> 00:05:41.487
- Right, Scoob?
- I know I am.


00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:44.433
Punch buggy white.


00:05:44.635 --> 00:05:48.071
Ouch. Oh, good one, Scoob.


00:05:48.238 --> 00:05:51.605
But it's a shame you didn't notice
the punch buggy green.


00:05:51.775 --> 00:05:53.208
Ow!


00:05:55.145 --> 00:05:56.737
[SHAGGY & SCOOBY GRUNTING]


00:05:56.914 --> 00:05:59.405
- All right.
- You know what? That is it. I've had it.


00:05:59.583 --> 00:06:03.019
You know, I will turn this van around.


00:06:04.421 --> 00:06:06.582
- Do I have to come back there?
DAPHNE: Scooby-Doo...


00:06:06.757 --> 00:06:09.157
...get your tail out of my face.


00:06:10.394 --> 00:06:13.192
DAPHNE: Fred, where are those
directions I sent you to print out?


00:06:13.397 --> 00:06:17.197
Don't worry, we're not lost.


00:06:22.773 --> 00:06:26.300
DAPHNE: Hm. This sure doesn't look
like my uncle's country club.


00:06:27.444 --> 00:06:30.311
Oh. Hey, look. It's the S.S. Daphne.


00:06:31.381 --> 00:06:33.281
DAPHNE:
Ha, ha.


00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:35.975
Oh, look. Try stopping there, sweetie.


00:06:36.219 --> 00:06:38.414
FRED:
Whatever you say, dear.


00:06:47.264 --> 00:06:49.596
VELMA:
Oh, how quaint.


00:06:59.609 --> 00:07:00.633
Hm.


00:07:00.811 --> 00:07:02.802
Hello?


00:07:03.013 --> 00:07:05.243
Anybody home?


00:07:05.449 --> 00:07:08.748
Like, yikes. Maybe we ought to just find
our own way...


00:07:08.919 --> 00:07:11.012
...to your uncle's country club.


00:07:12.289 --> 00:07:13.313
Zoinks!


00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:14.684
Country club?


00:07:14.858 --> 00:07:17.952
You're going to the country club?


00:07:18.128 --> 00:07:20.028
Yes, we have summer jobs there.


00:07:20.263 --> 00:07:24.529
No, you must turn back.
You must leave while you still can.


00:07:24.735 --> 00:07:28.694
- Leave? Why would we wanna leave?
- They were fools to build there.


00:07:28.872 --> 00:07:30.032
I tried to warn them...


00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:32.640
...but they thought
I was just some crazy hag.


00:07:32.809 --> 00:07:35.107
You? Heh. No.


00:07:35.312 --> 00:07:39.510
But mark my words,
the lake monster will return.


00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:43.743
The lake monster will return.


00:07:44.755 --> 00:07:46.814
[WHIMPERING]


00:07:47.524 --> 00:07:49.617
- Did you get directions?
- Uh....


00:07:49.793 --> 00:07:51.693
- Not exactly.
SHAGGY: Oh, yes, we did.


00:07:51.895 --> 00:07:54.989
Make a U-turn
and head straight back to Coolsville.


00:07:55.198 --> 00:07:58.634
There's a monster at the lake, guys.
A monster.


00:07:58.835 --> 00:08:00.996
- A monster?
- Mm-hm.


00:08:01.204 --> 00:08:04.298
Would you be referring
to the lake monster of Erie Pointe?


00:08:04.875 --> 00:08:07.343
You know, I didn't catch his name.


00:08:07.511 --> 00:08:10.639
- All I heard was "monster."
VELMA: No, look.


00:08:12.382 --> 00:08:15.977
It says here for hundreds of years
there have been sightings...


00:08:16.153 --> 00:08:19.919
...of hideous creatures
said to live at the bottom of the lake.


00:08:20.157 --> 00:08:23.820
I get it, it's one of those things
like Bigfoot or the Loch Ness monster.


00:08:24.027 --> 00:08:27.155
Oh, no, it's worse than we thought.


00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:30.424
No, Shaggy, I think what Fred means
is that it's just a legend.


00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:34.001
You know, lots of small towns
make them up. They're good for tourism.


00:08:34.438 --> 00:08:37.601
Oh. Oh, sure, you know,
come for the scenery...


00:08:37.808 --> 00:08:40.208
...stay for the certain death.


00:08:40.844 --> 00:08:41.868
[THUD]


00:08:42.045 --> 00:08:44.707
Come on, guys. Let's just get going
or we're gonna be late.


00:08:46.883 --> 00:08:48.612
Uh, Fred?


00:08:49.319 --> 00:08:52.550
- We still don't know how to get there.
- Mm-hm.


00:08:52.722 --> 00:08:57.022
Actually, yes, we do.


00:08:57.360 --> 00:08:58.588
[SHAGGY SIGHS]


00:08:58.762 --> 00:09:00.229
- No.
- Yes.


00:09:12.542 --> 00:09:14.032
FRED:
Pretty swank, Daph.


00:09:14.211 --> 00:09:18.204
DAPHNE: Yeah, looks like my uncle
really outdid himself this time.


00:09:22.219 --> 00:09:23.982
Thanks, Shaggy.


00:09:24.554 --> 00:09:25.578
[LAUGHS]


00:09:25.755 --> 00:09:29.748
- Is that my favorite niece?
- Uncle Thorny.


00:09:31.428 --> 00:09:32.725
Wow.


00:09:34.131 --> 00:09:36.156
Thank you again, uncle.


00:09:36.366 --> 00:09:39.267
I don't know what we would've done
without these summer jobs.


00:09:39.436 --> 00:09:42.337
Yeah. And, again, just for the record...


00:09:42.506 --> 00:09:45.475
...it's a well-known fact
that scarecrows are afraid of fire--


00:09:45.642 --> 00:09:46.666
[SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY]


00:09:46.877 --> 00:09:49.903
Gang, I'd like you to meet
Thorton Blake IV.


00:09:50.080 --> 00:09:51.445
Fifth, actually.


00:09:51.615 --> 00:09:53.378
Uncle Thorny, this is the gang.


00:09:53.583 --> 00:09:54.607
This is Shaggy.


00:09:54.784 --> 00:09:55.944
- Hi.
- Hi.


00:09:56.119 --> 00:09:57.780
- Fred.
- Oh.


00:09:58.255 --> 00:09:59.654
DAPHNE: Velma.
- Pleasure.


00:09:59.823 --> 00:10:01.256
- And--
SCOOBY: Scooby-Doo.


00:10:01.424 --> 00:10:02.982
Nice to meet you, Uncle Thorny.


00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:05.025
Smile.


00:10:05.195 --> 00:10:06.890
[SCOOBY GIGGLES]


00:10:07.597 --> 00:10:10.828
Well, I'm sure glad to have you all
on board this summer.


00:10:11.034 --> 00:10:15.471
Grab your stuff, get settled,
and park that thing in the back.


00:10:15.639 --> 00:10:18.802
Oh. You're gonna need
to get a good night's sleep.


00:10:18.975 --> 00:10:22.638
Your shifts start at 6 a.m. sharp.


00:10:23.914 --> 00:10:25.609
There's a 6 a.m.?


00:10:26.650 --> 00:10:27.674
[SIGHS]


00:10:29.519 --> 00:10:32.352
And that one. It's my makeup.


00:10:35.525 --> 00:10:37.288
[SHAGGY GRUNTING]


00:10:37.460 --> 00:10:40.861
- Shaggy, need a hand?
- No, thanks, Fred. I got it.


00:10:41.031 --> 00:10:43.727
It just takes a little elbow grease.


00:10:43.934 --> 00:10:45.458
[GASPING]


00:10:45.635 --> 00:10:46.932
Shaggy.


00:10:49.940 --> 00:10:54.172
Shaggy, are you all right?


00:10:54.878 --> 00:10:57.346
Like, I am now.


00:10:58.248 --> 00:10:59.545
Shaggy.


00:11:00.317 --> 00:11:02.080
Yes, Velma?


00:11:02.319 --> 00:11:06.312
I don't know how much longer
I can hold you.


00:11:18.068 --> 00:11:20.093
- Hey, Scoob?
- Huh?


00:11:21.504 --> 00:11:24.268
- Can I talk to you man-to-man?
- Uh....


00:11:24.474 --> 00:11:26.499
Sort of.


00:11:26.710 --> 00:11:30.077
I think I might have just had
a hayloft moment with Velma.


00:11:31.281 --> 00:11:33.715
Do you think it's possible that--?


00:11:33.883 --> 00:11:39.753
I don't know,
that she and I are meant to be?


00:11:40.590 --> 00:11:42.717
[LAUGHING]


00:11:46.062 --> 00:11:48.758
Yeah. Thanks for the support, pal.


00:11:48.999 --> 00:11:51.695
I'll remember this come flea season.


00:11:54.104 --> 00:11:56.197
[PUFFING]


00:11:59.242 --> 00:12:01.301
[CONTINUES LAUGHING]


00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:08.417
[TREE BRANCHES RUSTLE]


00:12:09.252 --> 00:12:12.380
Getting much better distance
on those woods, sir.


00:12:13.089 --> 00:12:18.117
Hey, Fred,
can I talk to you man-to-man?


00:12:18.795 --> 00:12:20.456
Sort of.


00:12:21.064 --> 00:12:25.592
Well, you and Daphne,
is that something you recommend?


00:12:25.769 --> 00:12:27.396
What do you mean?


00:12:27.570 --> 00:12:30.130
Well, you know, going from having...


00:12:30.307 --> 00:12:33.970
...you know, a girl friend
to a girlfriend.


00:12:34.144 --> 00:12:38.410
Heh, heh. I don't know if I'd really
call Daphne my girlfriend, Shags.


00:12:38.581 --> 00:12:41.106
You know, it's more casual than that.
We're just, um....


00:12:41.284 --> 00:12:43.616
- We're hanging out.
- Hanging out?


00:12:43.787 --> 00:12:46.517
No, Fred is totally my boyfriend.


00:12:46.690 --> 00:12:47.987
Really?


00:12:48.158 --> 00:12:51.252
I always thought football players
liked to, well...


00:12:51.428 --> 00:12:53.419
- ...play the field.
- Pfft.


00:12:53.596 --> 00:12:58.659
Me too. I never thought Fred would
be the relationship type, but he totally is.


00:12:58.868 --> 00:13:00.529
I'm just not the relationship type.


00:13:00.704 --> 00:13:03.969
I'm a football player,
we like to, uh, play the field.


00:13:04.140 --> 00:13:05.971
Anyhow, it's summer, Shaggy.


00:13:06.142 --> 00:13:09.009
Oh, yeah, summer. Totally.


00:13:09.779 --> 00:13:13.943
Because who'd want a girlfriend
during daylight-savings time?


00:13:15.018 --> 00:13:16.679
Good guess, but what I'm saying...


00:13:16.853 --> 00:13:20.016
...is summer's a time you just wanna
have fun. Not get so serious.


00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:22.522
Daphne's cool,
she feels the same way.


00:13:22.692 --> 00:13:24.887
It's totally getting serious.


00:13:25.095 --> 00:13:27.290
Fred's cool, he feels the same way.


00:13:27.464 --> 00:13:31.662
Well, it certainly sounds
like you two are perfectly in sync.


00:13:31.835 --> 00:13:32.893
Yeah.


00:13:33.103 --> 00:13:35.094
- Exactly.
- Exactly.


00:13:35.305 --> 00:13:37.364
[SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY]


00:13:38.675 --> 00:13:40.734
[YAWNS]


00:13:42.979 --> 00:13:44.207
SHAGGY:
Hey, Scoob.


00:13:44.414 --> 00:13:49.374
- How was the first dog day of summer?
- Relaxing.


00:13:49.619 --> 00:13:52.349
Glad to hear it, boy.
Now, come on, let's go get some--


00:13:52.522 --> 00:13:55.719
Oh, hello, Velma.


00:13:55.925 --> 00:13:59.088
- How was your day?
- Fine, I guess.


00:13:59.262 --> 00:14:02.561
Oh, really? Like, mine was fine too.


00:14:02.732 --> 00:14:05.257
It's crazy
how much we have in common, huh?


00:14:05.835 --> 00:14:06.927
Oh, boy.


00:14:07.137 --> 00:14:10.265
So, guys, my uncle invited us
to the opening night reception.


00:14:10.440 --> 00:14:12.601
- What do you say?
- Awesome.


00:14:12.776 --> 00:14:15.176
- How about a dip in the pool first?
DAPHNE: Sounds great.


00:14:17.514 --> 00:14:21.382
Oh, like, that sounds like a real rager.
What do you think, V?


00:14:21.584 --> 00:14:24.417
Perhaps I'll rendezvous
with everyone later.


00:14:24.654 --> 00:14:29.148
Since we arrived, I've been eager
to survey the indigenous flora and fauna.


00:14:29.926 --> 00:14:31.951
Oh, hey. Wait up.


00:14:32.162 --> 00:14:35.791
So you say there's both flora and fauna
out there, huh?


00:14:35.965 --> 00:14:39.901
When was the last time you heard
those two things in the same sentence?


00:14:41.304 --> 00:14:42.362
[BELCHES]


00:14:43.373 --> 00:14:47.434
Shaggy, did you know
Lake Erie is the warmest...


00:14:47.677 --> 00:14:51.044
...and most biologically productive
of the Great Lakes?


00:14:51.214 --> 00:14:54.809
Not to mention
the eleventh largest lake in the world.


00:14:54.984 --> 00:14:56.042
[METAL DETECTOR BEEPING]


00:14:56.219 --> 00:14:57.584
SHAGGY:
Oh, wow.


00:14:58.121 --> 00:15:01.557
I could listen to you talk like that
for hours.


00:15:02.625 --> 00:15:05.253
Are you really interested
in this stuff, Shaggy?


00:15:06.229 --> 00:15:11.292
I've never known you to be,
well, intellectually curious.


00:15:12.936 --> 00:15:15.427
Oh, I'm curious
about a lot of things, Velma.


00:15:15.638 --> 00:15:16.935
Like....


00:15:17.106 --> 00:15:19.666
Like people and relationships...


00:15:19.843 --> 00:15:23.335
...and relationships between people.


00:15:28.017 --> 00:15:29.917
Hey.


00:15:31.454 --> 00:15:33.115
[GRUNTING]


00:15:34.090 --> 00:15:37.787
Hey, Shaggy,
you're gonna love this factoid.


00:15:38.328 --> 00:15:42.162
Lake Erie has been gradually rising
over the last few hundred years.


00:15:42.365 --> 00:15:46.426
That means beneath
all of these rock formations...


00:15:46.603 --> 00:15:49.003
...there are miles
of underwater caves.


00:15:49.239 --> 00:15:51.833
- Get out of town.
- No, really.


00:15:52.008 --> 00:15:54.806
You can tell
by the variegated sedimentary striations.


00:15:55.445 --> 00:15:57.675
Oh, would you look at that.


00:15:57.847 --> 00:16:02.841
I've never seen irrigated rudimentary
claymations like that before.


00:16:03.953 --> 00:16:09.118
Hey, Velma, yesterday at the van....


00:16:09.459 --> 00:16:10.687
Uh....


00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:12.350
Jinkies.


00:16:12.896 --> 00:16:15.694
Look at this, Shaggy.


00:16:15.899 --> 00:16:18.891
I think it might actually
be a moonstone.


00:16:19.068 --> 00:16:20.797
They're very rare.


00:16:21.004 --> 00:16:22.995
You know,
the Native Americans believed...


00:16:23.172 --> 00:16:27.802
...they held this mystical connection
with the moon, thereby the name.


00:16:29.779 --> 00:16:32.179
Look at how it glows.


00:16:32.982 --> 00:16:35.576
It's beautiful, isn't it?


00:16:37.287 --> 00:16:39.221
It sure is.


00:16:39.389 --> 00:16:42.017
Almost as beautiful as your eyes.


00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:46.927
- Oh, Shaggy.
- Oh, Velma.


00:16:47.096 --> 00:16:50.224
Oh, Shaggy, I think I'm gonna be sick.


00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:54.803
- What? Oh, Velma, are you all right?
- I'm fine.


00:16:55.204 --> 00:16:57.502
I just feel really nauseous
all of a sudden.


00:16:57.707 --> 00:16:59.504
SHAGGY:
Like, you better sit down.


00:16:59.709 --> 00:17:01.700
- Here, let me help.
- No, it's okay.


00:17:02.078 --> 00:17:05.912
I'm just gonna go back to the room
and lie down for a little while.


00:17:07.216 --> 00:17:09.377
Oh, okay.


00:17:17.193 --> 00:17:19.525
I think she likes me.


00:17:19.762 --> 00:17:21.889
Oy vay.


00:17:24.834 --> 00:17:26.893
[PIANO PLAYING]


00:17:27.103 --> 00:17:30.095
THORNY: Well, I'll catch you out there
on the links, huh?


00:17:30.273 --> 00:17:31.535
Oh.


00:17:31.708 --> 00:17:35.109
Senator. I'm so glad
you could make it.


00:17:35.278 --> 00:17:40.375
Oh, how could I ever say no
to my biggest contributor?


00:17:40.550 --> 00:17:42.074
- How about a photograph?
- Yes.


00:17:46.089 --> 00:17:49.581
- Good thing I dressed up, hey, Scoob?
SCOOBY: Yeah.


00:17:49.759 --> 00:17:52.751
Hey, Shagg, Scoob. Where's Velma?


00:17:52.929 --> 00:17:54.328
Oh. Uh, heh.


00:17:54.497 --> 00:17:58.763
Uh, she got sick all of a sudden.
But it was totally natural causes...


00:17:58.935 --> 00:18:01.165
...and not revulsion
at the very thought of me.


00:18:02.138 --> 00:18:03.264
Okay.


00:18:06.909 --> 00:18:10.811
- Hey, Scoob, check out the buffet.
- Ooh.


00:18:11.781 --> 00:18:15.239
Now, if you don't mind,
one from my best side.


00:18:16.486 --> 00:18:17.748
One more.


00:18:22.625 --> 00:18:25.253
This will be good in my scrapbook.


00:18:26.396 --> 00:18:28.125
Perfect.


00:18:44.213 --> 00:18:46.681
Like, who ordered the pea soup?


00:18:55.358 --> 00:18:57.155
THORNY:
Sorry, everyone.


00:18:57.360 --> 00:19:00.796
I'm sure it's just a little minor glitch
with one of our generators.


00:19:00.963 --> 00:19:02.191
I'll just--


00:19:02.932 --> 00:19:03.956
[GROWLING]


00:19:04.133 --> 00:19:05.828
What the heck is that?


00:19:06.035 --> 00:19:08.128
[GASPING]


00:19:10.940 --> 00:19:13.500
- Fred?
- I don't know either, Daph.


00:19:19.348 --> 00:19:20.508
[WOMAN SCREAMS]


00:19:20.683 --> 00:19:22.173
[ROARING]


00:19:22.351 --> 00:19:25.650
SCOOBY:
Lake monster.


00:19:27.457 --> 00:19:30.858
Excuse me, I don't recall
having seen your name on the guest list.


00:19:42.071 --> 00:19:44.062
[SCREAMING]


00:19:49.912 --> 00:19:51.277
[PHOTOGRAPHER SCREAMS]


00:19:55.017 --> 00:19:57.247
That thing can't be real, can it?


00:19:57.420 --> 00:20:01.117
I don't know, but I'm not
getting close enough to find out.


00:20:02.191 --> 00:20:03.249
Hi.


00:20:05.995 --> 00:20:07.758
[ROARS]


00:20:14.504 --> 00:20:15.528
THORNY:
No, please.


00:20:15.705 --> 00:20:16.729
Please, everyone...


00:20:16.906 --> 00:20:20.034
...I'm sure there's a logical explanation
as to what's going on.


00:20:20.209 --> 00:20:21.642
We'll just tidy up the tent...


00:20:21.811 --> 00:20:25.076
...and, you know,
we'll just continue the party.


00:20:25.248 --> 00:20:26.772
Everyone-- Oh, senator, senator.


00:20:26.949 --> 00:20:30.214
MAN: Give me the keys, I'll get it myself.
WOMAN: Just go without him.


00:20:30.720 --> 00:20:32.017
My goodness.


00:20:32.755 --> 00:20:36.452
Why do I have the feeling
I missed something rather significant?


00:20:36.626 --> 00:20:40.027
It was the lake monster.
The lake monster of Erie Pointe.


00:20:40.229 --> 00:20:44.632
It was horrifying, terrifying,
scariest thing I've ever seen in my life.


00:20:44.801 --> 00:20:48.134
On a more personal note,
how are you feeling, Velma?


00:20:48.304 --> 00:20:51.762
- Did you just say the lake monster?
- Yeah.


00:20:51.941 --> 00:20:52.999
You can't be serious.


00:20:53.176 --> 00:20:56.270
Oh, my guests sure seemed to think
it was serious.


00:20:56.445 --> 00:20:58.072
Look at this, not even day one...


00:20:58.247 --> 00:21:00.738
...and half of them
have canceled their memberships.


00:21:00.917 --> 00:21:03.977
If somebody doesn't figure out
what's going on here quickly...


00:21:04.153 --> 00:21:06.951
...it's gonna be a very short summer
for all of us.


00:21:08.057 --> 00:21:10.855
Guys, we have to do something.


00:21:11.060 --> 00:21:14.188
We can't afford to lose these jobs.


00:21:22.772 --> 00:21:23.796
Oh, no.


00:21:23.973 --> 00:21:25.304
No, no, no.


00:21:25.474 --> 00:21:27.499
- You guys thinking what I'm thinking?
- No.


00:21:27.677 --> 00:21:29.611
- Come on.
- Guys, please, don't--


00:21:29.979 --> 00:21:31.003
[SIGHS]


00:21:31.180 --> 00:21:33.080
Here we go again.


00:21:33.282 --> 00:21:35.079
Uncle Thorny.


00:21:36.485 --> 00:21:39.113
We just wanna let you know
not to worry.


00:21:39.288 --> 00:21:41.017
Not only did you hire summer help...


00:21:41.190 --> 00:21:45.388
...you also hired the best supernatural
detectives in the tristate area.


00:21:45.628 --> 00:21:47.687
- I did?
- That's right.


00:21:47.864 --> 00:21:50.059
And I know just where to start too.


00:21:50.233 --> 00:21:52.531
With Elmer Uggins,
the person who's taken...


00:21:52.702 --> 00:21:55.364
...the only known photo
of the lake monster.


00:22:10.686 --> 00:22:13.154
FRED:
Heh. Would you look at that.


00:22:13.322 --> 00:22:17.224
Our first suspect just happens to be
the keeper of a creepy old lighthouse.


00:22:17.426 --> 00:22:19.053
You know, just once...


00:22:19.228 --> 00:22:24.029
...I wish we found a mystery
that started in a cheery futon showroom.


00:22:24.734 --> 00:22:25.996
What?


00:22:26.168 --> 00:22:30.332
Futons offer far more support
than traditional mattresses.


00:22:36.512 --> 00:22:38.571
[FOGHORN BLOWS]


00:22:51.460 --> 00:22:54.554
Well, looks like the light's on
but nobody's home.


00:22:54.730 --> 00:22:57.927
Isn't this the part when we normally
split up and search for clues?


00:22:58.100 --> 00:23:00.091
I'll go with Velma. Ha.


00:23:01.704 --> 00:23:03.604
Come on. It'll be fun.


00:23:04.540 --> 00:23:07.703
Okay. Come on, Daph.


00:23:14.784 --> 00:23:16.445
[SHAGGY SNIFFING]


00:23:16.619 --> 00:23:21.454
Oh, Velma, what is that sweet fragrance
you're wearing?


00:23:21.924 --> 00:23:23.619
Bug and tick repellent.


00:23:23.793 --> 00:23:24.987
[MOSQUITO BUZZING]


00:23:25.194 --> 00:23:28.595
Well, it certainly isn't repelling me.


00:23:33.803 --> 00:23:35.270
[CLEARS THROAT]


00:23:36.772 --> 00:23:39.570
It sure is a lovely night, huh?


00:23:39.742 --> 00:23:42.677
I've always enjoyed
strolling beneath a full moon.


00:23:42.845 --> 00:23:45.973
Werewolves notwithstanding,
of course.


00:23:46.415 --> 00:23:50.442
I too enjoy walking
by the light of the silvery moon.


00:23:50.619 --> 00:23:51.745
[CHUCKLES]


00:23:51.921 --> 00:23:55.322
Heh, heh, heh.
Yeah, that's a good one.


00:23:55.491 --> 00:23:57.152
Wait, where's the funny?


00:23:57.827 --> 00:24:00.523
- Oh. "By the Light of the Silvery Moon"?
- Yeah.


00:24:00.730 --> 00:24:03.528
It's just an old vaudevillian ditty.


00:24:03.766 --> 00:24:07.497
But I must confess,
I do have a soft spot for it.


00:24:09.972 --> 00:24:14.341
Like, wait, I think I do know that one.


00:24:21.650 --> 00:24:24.278
- [SINGING] By the light
CHORUS: Not the dark, but the light


00:24:24.453 --> 00:24:27.718
- Of the silvery moon
CHORUS: Not the sun, but the moon


00:24:27.890 --> 00:24:31.121
- I wanna spoon
CHORUS: Not broom, but spoon


00:24:31.293 --> 00:24:35.855
To my honey I'll croon love's tune


00:24:36.032 --> 00:24:38.899
- Honeymoon
- Honeymoon, honeymoon


00:24:39.068 --> 00:24:42.003
- Keep a-shining in June
- Keep a-shining in June


00:24:42.171 --> 00:24:45.732
Your silvery beams
Will bring love's dreams


00:24:45.908 --> 00:24:48.809
We'll be cuddling soon


00:24:49.278 --> 00:24:53.009
By the light of the silvery


00:24:53.315 --> 00:24:57.479
CHORUS: Moon
SHAGGY: Moon


00:24:57.720 --> 00:24:59.813
[RECORD SCRATCHING]


00:25:00.056 --> 00:25:02.354
ALL [SINGING]:
Act one, scene new


00:25:02.525 --> 00:25:05.016
Act two
Me, you


00:25:05.194 --> 00:25:07.185
Let's go
New tune


00:25:07.363 --> 00:25:09.160
- By the light
- Not the dark, but the light


00:25:09.331 --> 00:25:11.925
- Of the silvery moon
- Not the sun, but the moon


00:25:12.101 --> 00:25:14.262
- I wanna spoon
- Not broom, but spoon


00:25:14.437 --> 00:25:17.235
- To my honey I'll croon
- Croon! Five, six


00:25:17.406 --> 00:25:19.431
- By the moon
- By the moon, by the moon


00:25:19.608 --> 00:25:21.872
- Keep it shining in June
- Keep it shining in June


00:25:22.044 --> 00:25:24.376
Your silvery beams
Will bring love's dreams


00:25:24.547 --> 00:25:27.015
- We'll be cuddling soon
- We'll be cuddling soon


00:25:27.183 --> 00:25:30.016
By the silvery moon


00:25:42.932 --> 00:25:47.301
Hey, Fred, you don't think Shaggy
could have a crush on Velma, do you?


00:25:47.470 --> 00:25:50.735
Not unless she turned into
a steaming bowl of chili cheese fries.


00:25:50.906 --> 00:25:52.373
[CHUCKLES]


00:25:53.576 --> 00:25:55.908
- Why?
- I don't know, it's just...


00:25:56.078 --> 00:25:58.376
...he's been acting really goofy lately.


00:25:58.547 --> 00:26:00.208
Even for Shaggy.


00:26:00.382 --> 00:26:03.476
And he's been following Velma around
like a puppy dog.


00:26:03.652 --> 00:26:06.280
Actually, that would explain
why he's been asking me...


00:26:06.455 --> 00:26:08.446
...all those questions about dating.


00:26:08.624 --> 00:26:11.320
But I guess he didn't take my advice.


00:26:11.494 --> 00:26:14.088
Advice? Wait, Fred, what advice?


00:26:19.001 --> 00:26:20.468
[CREATURE GROWLING]


00:26:21.370 --> 00:26:26.398
Um, Velma, that wasn't what I thought
it was, was it?


00:26:26.575 --> 00:26:27.837
I don't know.


00:26:28.010 --> 00:26:32.777
Did you surmise that it was a heretofore
unclassified amphibious humanoid?


00:26:33.282 --> 00:26:38.185
No. I thought it was a lake monster!
Zoinks!


00:26:38.387 --> 00:26:39.786
Fred?


00:26:39.955 --> 00:26:43.584
Exactly what advice
did you give Shaggy about dating?


00:26:43.759 --> 00:26:44.783
What?


00:26:44.960 --> 00:26:49.158
Oh, you know, just that it's summertime
and we're not really--


00:26:49.331 --> 00:26:50.423
[CREATURE ROARS]


00:26:50.599 --> 00:26:51.691
Come on.


00:26:51.934 --> 00:26:53.834
Go, go, go!


00:26:54.036 --> 00:26:56.834
SHAGGY:
It's the lake monster! Save me.


00:26:57.039 --> 00:26:59.337
MONSTER:
Ow! My ankle.


00:26:59.508 --> 00:27:01.100
What?


00:27:05.281 --> 00:27:06.339
UGGINS:
Hey.


00:27:06.949 --> 00:27:08.541
Mr. Uggins, I presume?


00:27:12.521 --> 00:27:14.148
Call me Elmer.


00:27:15.958 --> 00:27:17.289
Hi, kids.


00:27:19.828 --> 00:27:23.525
So you've never actually seen
the monster?


00:27:23.699 --> 00:27:26.896
I was just using the legend
to make a quick buck.


00:27:27.069 --> 00:27:29.333
Made some postcards...


00:27:29.538 --> 00:27:32.166
...sold them to the local tourist traps.


00:27:32.942 --> 00:27:34.136
- Mm?
- No.


00:27:34.310 --> 00:27:36.175
- No.
- Thanks.


00:27:36.879 --> 00:27:37.903
Hey, what can I say?


00:27:38.080 --> 00:27:40.844
You know, lighthouse keeping
ain't exactly a growth industry.


00:27:41.016 --> 00:27:42.540
[CHUCKLING]


00:27:43.219 --> 00:27:44.743
Ahem. Anyway...


00:27:44.954 --> 00:27:48.549
...when I heard about all the hoopla
down at the country club tonight...


00:27:48.724 --> 00:27:53.218
...I figured it might be a good time
to dust off old green-eyes over there...


00:27:53.462 --> 00:27:54.986
...and take some new shots.


00:27:55.164 --> 00:27:56.722
[IMITATING CAMERA SHUTTER
CLICKING]


00:27:56.899 --> 00:27:58.230
But listen, kids...


00:27:58.467 --> 00:28:01.994
...if this thing's really back,
you best leave now while you still can.


00:28:02.204 --> 00:28:05.196
Come on, you don't really believe
the monster's real, do you?


00:28:05.407 --> 00:28:07.875
It's probably some prankster
with a better costume.


00:28:08.043 --> 00:28:10.170
Maybe it is and maybe it ain't.


00:28:10.346 --> 00:28:12.405
But one thing's for sure...


00:28:12.581 --> 00:28:16.381
...the legend is a truly terrible tale.


00:28:16.552 --> 00:28:21.012
It all goes back
to the very beginnings of town.


00:28:21.223 --> 00:28:24.351
When the first settlers arrived
in these parts...


00:28:24.526 --> 00:28:27.290
...they was confronted
by an old woman...


00:28:27.496 --> 00:28:30.693
...who was said to live
in a cave by the lake.


00:28:30.899 --> 00:28:32.696
Grubwort was her name.


00:28:32.901 --> 00:28:34.869
Wanda Grubwort.


00:28:35.037 --> 00:28:37.870
She claimed all the land around the lake
belonged to her...


00:28:38.040 --> 00:28:41.100
...and told the settlers that
if they didn't turn back...


00:28:41.644 --> 00:28:43.771
...they would pay the price.


00:28:44.380 --> 00:28:47.872
But them early pioneers was not about
to be turned away so easily...


00:28:48.050 --> 00:28:53.955
...so they settled in
and forgot all about her warning.


00:28:54.323 --> 00:28:57.884
But Wanda Grubwort did not forget.


00:28:58.060 --> 00:29:03.327
And one day,
she fulfilled her dark oath.


00:29:04.833 --> 00:29:07.631
Using her magical staff...


00:29:07.836 --> 00:29:11.795
...she cast a spell
upon an innocent creature of the lake...


00:29:12.675 --> 00:29:16.907
...transforming it into a hideous beast.


00:29:21.684 --> 00:29:24.414
Once Grubwort
had her monstrous slave...


00:29:24.586 --> 00:29:27.350
...she loosed it upon the villagers.


00:29:34.296 --> 00:29:37.288
And then? What happened next?


00:29:37.466 --> 00:29:41.459
Well, it's said the settlers
eventually overcame Grubwort...


00:29:41.637 --> 00:29:46.370
...tried her for witchery
and burned her at the stake.


00:29:49.178 --> 00:29:50.839
Like I said...


00:29:52.281 --> 00:29:55.444
...you best leave now
while you still can.


00:29:56.985 --> 00:29:59.818
I'm sorry, Mr. Uggins,
but we just don't give up that easy.


00:30:00.656 --> 00:30:04.524
He obviously wasn't
in my sophomore geometry class.


00:30:06.095 --> 00:30:07.528
[UGGINS GRUNTS]


00:30:08.464 --> 00:30:12.696
SHAGGY:
Mr. Shaggy...


00:30:13.836 --> 00:30:15.895
...Dinkley.


00:30:16.138 --> 00:30:18.606
It's like the angels are singing it.


00:30:19.141 --> 00:30:21.632
- Mister--
- Hey, Shagg. What you doing?


00:30:22.745 --> 00:30:25.236
Oh! Um-- Nothing.


00:30:32.321 --> 00:30:36.917
Doctor says I need more linen
in my diet.


00:30:37.993 --> 00:30:39.927
Okay. So, have you seen Fred?


00:30:41.063 --> 00:30:42.860
He's out on the--


00:30:43.065 --> 00:30:45.499
Out on the green,
putting with some girls.


00:30:46.335 --> 00:30:47.359
Girls?


00:30:47.536 --> 00:30:50.232
FRED:
Now, just remember to follow through.


00:30:50.739 --> 00:30:52.832
GIRL 1:
Follow through.


00:30:54.943 --> 00:30:56.774
Hey.


00:30:57.012 --> 00:30:59.173
GIRL 1: Thanks.
FRED: Okay, guys, I'm out of here.


00:30:59.915 --> 00:31:02.110
- Okay, I'll see you guys later.
- Bye.


00:31:02.284 --> 00:31:04.752
GIRL 2: Bye, Fred.
FRED: Bye now.


00:31:06.221 --> 00:31:07.586
Hey, Daph.


00:31:07.790 --> 00:31:09.451
- What's up, Shags?
- Hey, Fred.


00:31:12.961 --> 00:31:14.189
What?


00:31:14.363 --> 00:31:16.160
Hey, um...


00:31:16.932 --> 00:31:19.025
...can I ask your advice
about something?


00:31:19.201 --> 00:31:20.600
Sure.


00:31:20.803 --> 00:31:22.930
Well, I....


00:31:24.206 --> 00:31:26.197
See, I have this friend, okay?


00:31:26.375 --> 00:31:29.742
His name's, um, Scruffy. Yeah, Scruffy.
They call him that...


00:31:29.912 --> 00:31:33.109
...because he has a goatee.
No, that would be too obvious.


00:31:33.315 --> 00:31:38.719
Anyway, so this friend of mine,
who doesn't have a goatee or a dog...


00:31:38.921 --> 00:31:40.946
...definitely doesn't have
a dog either...


00:31:41.190 --> 00:31:44.682
...he has this crush on this girl
he sometimes solves mysteries with.


00:31:44.893 --> 00:31:46.986
No, no. That's a dead giveaway.


00:31:47.596 --> 00:31:49.826
- Let me start over. So--
- Shaggy.


00:31:50.566 --> 00:31:53.399
It's okay. We know you like Velma.


00:31:54.336 --> 00:31:55.394
[SCOFFS]


00:31:55.571 --> 00:31:56.833
Oh. Oh, what?


00:31:57.005 --> 00:31:59.337
Oh, I don't know
what you guys are talking about.


00:31:59.508 --> 00:32:01.908
I definitely do not like-- Velma.


00:32:02.077 --> 00:32:05.513
You are not gonna believe what I found
in the security footage. Come on.


00:32:08.750 --> 00:32:13.119
After you watch this,
I think you'll all be saying "jinkies."


00:32:14.456 --> 00:32:17.323
Hey, the security camera
caught the attack.


00:32:17.526 --> 00:32:20.825
Yep. And they caught
something else too.


00:32:24.833 --> 00:32:27.996
Looks like we have two pranksters
on our hands.


00:32:28.237 --> 00:32:29.636
Jinkies.


00:32:30.639 --> 00:32:32.937
- Told you.
- Freeze it.


00:32:33.108 --> 00:32:36.100
If you zoom in right here,
we can see who's inside that cloak.


00:32:41.850 --> 00:32:44.182
SHAGGY:
Oh, look, it's coming into focus.


00:32:45.053 --> 00:32:46.748
[SHAGGY SCREAMS]


00:32:47.656 --> 00:32:49.146
What happened?


00:32:49.324 --> 00:32:52.191
Like, that spooky figure
must be using some sort of magic...


00:32:52.361 --> 00:32:54.522
...to prevent us from seeing its face.


00:32:54.696 --> 00:33:00.066
I'm afraid the explanation is slightly
less supernatural than that, Shaggy.


00:33:00.302 --> 00:33:05.171
I accidentally knocked over my green tea
and short-circuited the hard drive.


00:33:05.674 --> 00:33:07.471
- Oh.
- That's okay, Velma.


00:33:07.676 --> 00:33:11.009
You know, I'm sure we'll find
another piece of critical evidence.


00:33:11.179 --> 00:33:12.646
- Right, guys?
- Yeah, for sure.


00:33:12.814 --> 00:33:14.145
- It's groovy.
FRED: Don't worry.


00:33:14.349 --> 00:33:17.284
I know this is highly
uncharacteristic behavior.


00:33:18.720 --> 00:33:21.086
I'm really sorry, guys.


00:33:25.928 --> 00:33:28.556
I'll tender my resignation from the group
if you wish.


00:33:28.730 --> 00:33:29.754
- What?
- What?


00:33:29.932 --> 00:33:30.990
DAPHNE: Velma.
- Come on.


00:33:31.166 --> 00:33:32.793
Velma.


00:33:35.437 --> 00:33:36.870
Like, hold on, V.


00:33:40.375 --> 00:33:44.744
Don't beat yourself up about this.
You just pulled a Shaggy, that's all.


00:33:45.514 --> 00:33:47.209
I do it all the time.


00:33:48.383 --> 00:33:51.682
Thanks, Shaggy,
but there's really no excuse.


00:33:52.688 --> 00:33:56.818
Maybe reading a little Sylvia Plath
will buoy my spirits.


00:33:57.759 --> 00:33:59.192
Hey, I....


00:33:59.361 --> 00:34:01.625
I still think you're wonderful.


00:34:01.830 --> 00:34:04.890
Shaggy, that was so nice.


00:34:05.100 --> 00:34:08.695
That's exactly how you should be
if you're really serious about Velma.


00:34:09.071 --> 00:34:11.096
Oh. Oh, what?


00:34:11.273 --> 00:34:13.207
Oh, what do you mean?


00:34:13.375 --> 00:34:14.865
I do not--


00:34:16.211 --> 00:34:17.872
All right, I admit it.


00:34:18.046 --> 00:34:19.445
I like Velma.


00:34:19.615 --> 00:34:22.846
I'm my friend. I'm Scruffy.


00:34:24.419 --> 00:34:26.284
But what am I gonna do?


00:34:26.455 --> 00:34:29.083
You know, I don't know
what I'm supposed to say to her.


00:34:29.257 --> 00:34:31.225
Let me help you out, Shags.


00:34:31.426 --> 00:34:33.121
You gotta be confident, smooth.


00:34:33.362 --> 00:34:35.227
- Girls like guys--
- Don't listen to him.


00:34:35.397 --> 00:34:37.456
He has no idea what girls like.


00:34:37.633 --> 00:34:40.227
See, what girls like is to feel special.


00:34:40.402 --> 00:34:42.768
To feel like they're the only one
on a guy's mind.


00:34:42.938 --> 00:34:45.304
Yeah, I know that.
But listen, what you wanna do--


00:34:45.474 --> 00:34:48.375
Well, if you know that,
then why don't you try it sometime?


00:34:48.577 --> 00:34:50.568
What's with you?
Why are you acting weird?


00:34:50.746 --> 00:34:53.613
- How exactly am I act--?
- Like, you know what?


00:34:53.815 --> 00:34:55.749
Forget I even asked.


00:34:55.951 --> 00:34:57.976
I'll just figure this out for myself.


00:34:58.153 --> 00:35:02.112
Besides, if I ever get Velma to like me,
I want it to be real...


00:35:02.290 --> 00:35:04.815
...not some loosey-goosey thing
like you guys have.


00:35:09.297 --> 00:35:11.527
Fred, did you say something
to Shaggy...


00:35:11.700 --> 00:35:14.999
...about us having
a "loosey-goosey" relationship?


00:35:15.203 --> 00:35:17.296
What? Oh, no, no.


00:35:18.040 --> 00:35:19.871
I just told him how we're casual.


00:35:20.042 --> 00:35:23.534
You know, how it's summer
and we're just hanging out.


00:35:24.346 --> 00:35:27.713
I mean,
that is what we're doing, right?


00:35:27.916 --> 00:35:31.977
Yes, Fred.
That is exactly what we're doing.


00:35:32.154 --> 00:35:38.024
I'm just so glad
that we're on the same page.


00:35:40.796 --> 00:35:44.823
Well, she's not the president
of the drama club for nothing.


00:35:45.934 --> 00:35:47.526
I like you, Velma Dinkley.


00:35:47.736 --> 00:35:49.203
So, what do you say?


00:35:49.438 --> 00:35:52.635
- Will you go on a date with me?
- Sorry, not my type.


00:35:52.808 --> 00:35:54.469
Like, come on, Scoob.


00:35:54.676 --> 00:35:57.076
Forget Velma.


00:35:57.946 --> 00:36:00.938
Time for a midnight snack.


00:36:01.383 --> 00:36:03.578
SHAGGY: A what?
- A midnight snack.


00:36:03.752 --> 00:36:08.382
You know, a couple of sandwiches,
a rack of ribs, pepperoni?


00:36:08.557 --> 00:36:12.493
- What?
- Oh, just follow me. Whew.


00:36:13.195 --> 00:36:14.321
Just my luck.


00:36:14.496 --> 00:36:18.091
I've got a talking dog
and I can't understand a word he says.


00:36:36.551 --> 00:36:38.610
SHAGGY:
Mm, mm, mm.


00:36:38.887 --> 00:36:41.856
Sandwich, look out.


00:36:43.625 --> 00:36:45.616
[SNIFFS THEN SIGHS]


00:36:45.794 --> 00:36:47.523
Is that Eau de' Dinkley I detect?


00:36:49.564 --> 00:36:50.758
Shaggy?


00:36:50.932 --> 00:36:55.562
Shaggy? Hey, what about
my midnight snack?


00:36:55.737 --> 00:36:57.796
[GROWLS]


00:36:59.407 --> 00:37:00.704
Huh.


00:37:01.109 --> 00:37:02.872
DAPHNE:
Nice shot.


00:37:15.157 --> 00:37:16.886
Mine.


00:37:17.092 --> 00:37:18.582
[MAN GRUNTS
AND DAPHNE SHRIEKS]


00:37:31.907 --> 00:37:33.932
Velma?


00:37:36.945 --> 00:37:39.140
Where is she?


00:37:46.154 --> 00:37:47.178
[TWIG CRACKS]


00:37:47.355 --> 00:37:48.822
[SIGHS]


00:37:52.828 --> 00:37:55.353
Oh, Velma, is that you?


00:37:58.800 --> 00:37:59.824
[ROARS]


00:38:00.202 --> 00:38:01.430
[SCREAMS]


00:38:04.840 --> 00:38:05.864
Oh, hi, Fred.


00:38:07.776 --> 00:38:09.107
Is something wrong?


00:38:09.311 --> 00:38:11.040
SHAGGY:
Help!


00:38:11.213 --> 00:38:13.511
- Help, help!
- Come on.


00:38:14.583 --> 00:38:15.845
- Shaggy.
- Aah!


00:38:16.017 --> 00:38:17.678
- What's wrong?
- Oh.


00:38:17.853 --> 00:38:19.514
Oh, you know, nothing.


00:38:19.688 --> 00:38:22.179
I just thought I'd work
on my blood-curdling scream.


00:38:22.357 --> 00:38:25.190
What the heck do you think is wrong?
It's the lake monster.


00:38:25.694 --> 00:38:26.718
Whoa!


00:38:28.530 --> 00:38:31.795
That's it, time to unmask this prankster
once and for all.


00:38:32.000 --> 00:38:34.093
[GRUNTING]


00:38:34.903 --> 00:38:37.531
Come on, help me with this mask.


00:38:41.109 --> 00:38:43.475
Fred, I don't think this thing
is a mask.


00:38:47.215 --> 00:38:50.116
Ew! Gross.


00:38:50.652 --> 00:38:52.620
FRED:
Keep moving.


00:38:54.923 --> 00:38:57.084
This thing keeps getting
the jump on us.


00:38:57.259 --> 00:39:00.353
It can't jump in two directions.
Come on, split up.


00:39:05.734 --> 00:39:07.361
Like, why did he have to pick me?


00:39:07.535 --> 00:39:10.504
In gym class,
I'm always the last one picked.


00:39:11.206 --> 00:39:12.230
Huh. Heh.


00:39:12.407 --> 00:39:14.068
Oh, zoinks.


00:39:14.242 --> 00:39:16.437
[ROARING]


00:39:20.548 --> 00:39:22.539
SCOOBY:
I'll save you, Shaggy.


00:39:26.187 --> 00:39:27.245
SHAGGY:
Like, thanks, buddy.


00:39:27.422 --> 00:39:30.152
I thought that giant mutant frog
was gonna make me croak.


00:39:30.358 --> 00:39:31.382
[SHAGGY GIGGLES]


00:39:31.559 --> 00:39:34.528
Oh, boy, I wish I could enjoy that one.


00:39:36.464 --> 00:39:39.024
Oh, heh. Oh. You did it, boy.


00:39:39.601 --> 00:39:40.863
Oh, what a friend.


00:39:41.036 --> 00:39:42.435
What a pal.


00:39:42.604 --> 00:39:43.696
What a sand trap.


00:39:44.105 --> 00:39:46.198
[BOTH SCREAMING]


00:39:52.447 --> 00:39:55.939
Oh, boy, Scoob.
I owe you one, buddy.


00:39:56.117 --> 00:39:58.745
If it wasn't for you, I would--


00:39:58.954 --> 00:40:01.616
Hey, would you look at that?


00:40:04.626 --> 00:40:06.821
- It's one of those moonstones.
- Yeah.


00:40:06.995 --> 00:40:10.590
Velma loves these things almost
as much I love deep-fried--


00:40:10.765 --> 00:40:12.562
Well, anything. Huh.


00:40:12.767 --> 00:40:14.496
Groovy.


00:40:14.803 --> 00:40:16.566
Huh? Hmph.


00:40:16.738 --> 00:40:19.639
Velma, Velma, Velma. Pfft.


00:40:22.711 --> 00:40:25.475
Hey, come on,
I think the coast is clear.


00:40:26.348 --> 00:40:29.476
This doesn't make sense.
There's no such thing as a lake monster.


00:40:29.651 --> 00:40:33.246
Tell that to the thing
that just threw up an aquarium.


00:40:33.521 --> 00:40:36.490
So now do you wanna tell me
who those guys were?


00:40:36.658 --> 00:40:38.023
Not now, Fred.


00:40:39.961 --> 00:40:42.020
[MONSTER GROWLING]


00:40:47.035 --> 00:40:49.868
Oh, that was worse than my date
with Herbie Zimmer.


00:40:50.105 --> 00:40:52.869
Totally, I-- Wait, you went on a date
with Herbie Zi--?


00:40:53.942 --> 00:40:56.001
[MONSTER SCREAMING]


00:41:08.456 --> 00:41:09.684
WOMAN:
Creature.


00:41:10.492 --> 00:41:13.655
What are you doing?
You're supposed to be searching.


00:41:13.828 --> 00:41:15.887
With all the bedlam
you've raised tonight...


00:41:16.064 --> 00:41:17.861
...we'll have to stop early.


00:41:18.033 --> 00:41:19.466
Return to the lake.


00:41:19.634 --> 00:41:23.263
I'll summon you
when it's safe to resume our search.


00:41:33.048 --> 00:41:34.345
[DAPHNE SIGHS]


00:41:34.883 --> 00:41:37.283
- That was close.
- Yeah.


00:41:39.154 --> 00:41:41.884
Hey. Not bad.


00:41:42.090 --> 00:41:43.557
[SIGHS]


00:41:44.426 --> 00:41:46.485
Uncle Thorny.


00:41:47.328 --> 00:41:48.659
That thing came back.


00:41:48.830 --> 00:41:51.094
Oh, you think?


00:41:52.934 --> 00:41:56.335
Canceled memberships
and now all this damage.


00:41:57.072 --> 00:42:00.838
I hate to say it, I may have no choice
but to shut this place down...


00:42:01.009 --> 00:42:04.570
...and go back to my life
as an international playboy.


00:42:07.615 --> 00:42:08.741
SHAGGY:
Hey, guys.


00:42:08.950 --> 00:42:10.440
Shaggy, you're okay.


00:42:10.618 --> 00:42:14.281
Well, yeah, I am,
but has anyone seen Velma?


00:42:14.456 --> 00:42:17.619
Before the monster attacked,
she was out here, I know it.


00:42:17.826 --> 00:42:18.918
Oh, no.


00:42:19.094 --> 00:42:21.756
Oh, you don't think the lake monster
got to her, do you?


00:42:21.930 --> 00:42:24.728
I've seen monster movies,
I know how this works.


00:42:24.899 --> 00:42:26.628
[ROARS THEN SCREAMS]


00:42:26.835 --> 00:42:29.804
Shaggy, Shaggy. Calm down, okay?


00:42:29.971 --> 00:42:31.302
- We're gonna find her.
- Yeah.


00:42:31.473 --> 00:42:32.531
- Let's go.
SHAGGY: Okay.


00:42:32.707 --> 00:42:35.232
FRED:
Velma!


00:42:36.978 --> 00:42:38.809
DAPHNE:
Velma!


00:42:38.980 --> 00:42:40.572
Velma?


00:42:40.748 --> 00:42:41.772
Where are you?


00:42:41.950 --> 00:42:44.851
- Velma!
- Velma!


00:42:46.721 --> 00:42:49.451
Hey, guys, I found her.


00:42:54.662 --> 00:42:57.961
- Oh, no. She's dead.
- Oh!


00:42:58.133 --> 00:43:00.727
Oh, she looks so peaceful.


00:43:00.902 --> 00:43:03.393
Oh, I can't look.


00:43:03.805 --> 00:43:04.931
[GROANS]


00:43:05.440 --> 00:43:07.874
Uh.... Guys?


00:43:10.612 --> 00:43:13.479
- What's going on?
- Oh, it's a miracle.


00:43:13.648 --> 00:43:16.276
FRED: What happened to you
last night, Velma?


00:43:16.684 --> 00:43:18.311
I don't know.


00:43:19.254 --> 00:43:22.883
I couldn't sleep,
so I went for a walk by the lake.


00:43:23.324 --> 00:43:25.519
But then that fog rolled in and....


00:43:26.794 --> 00:43:30.093
Well, I must have gotten lost.


00:43:30.265 --> 00:43:32.825
I sat down to wait until it lifted...


00:43:33.034 --> 00:43:35.298
...and I must have fallen asleep.


00:43:35.770 --> 00:43:38.170
Don't you ever do that to us again,
you hear?


00:43:38.339 --> 00:43:41.308
You had us all worried so--
What are those?


00:43:44.145 --> 00:43:47.012
- They kind of look like warts.
- Warts?


00:43:47.182 --> 00:43:48.774
Egads.


00:43:48.950 --> 00:43:50.815
Oh, no.


00:43:50.985 --> 00:43:56.821
I'm sure it's just some kind
of urushiol-induced dermatitis.


00:43:56.991 --> 00:43:58.982
- Oh.
- Yeah.


00:44:00.128 --> 00:44:03.222
Anyway, what's going on?


00:44:03.431 --> 00:44:06.628
You missed another attack.
Come on, we'll get you cleaned up...


00:44:06.801 --> 00:44:09.531
- ...and we'll fill you in.
VELMA: Another attack?


00:44:09.704 --> 00:44:12.502
Anybody else hungry? I know I am.


00:44:12.674 --> 00:44:13.800
Shocking.


00:44:14.008 --> 00:44:15.475
Mm.


00:44:16.177 --> 00:44:17.201
Ooh.


00:44:17.378 --> 00:44:20.211
So you think the monster's real
and someone's using it...


00:44:20.381 --> 00:44:21.871
...to dig up something
on the grounds?


00:44:22.050 --> 00:44:25.349
Yeah. Problem is, we don't have
a single clue about who's using it.


00:44:25.553 --> 00:44:30.684
Yes, we do. The mysterious figure
had a streak of purple paint on its cloak.


00:44:32.060 --> 00:44:34.995
- So?
- So remember the boat that we passed...


00:44:35.163 --> 00:44:38.428
...on the way up here?
Shaggy called it the S.S. Daphne.


00:44:38.600 --> 00:44:40.898
It was being painted
the exact same color.


00:44:41.102 --> 00:44:45.562
I'd be willing to bet that whoever's
behind this has been on that boat.


00:44:45.773 --> 00:44:47.866
All right, gang,
we know what we have to do.


00:44:48.343 --> 00:44:51.904
After our shifts tonight, we'll head
to the docks and we'll check it out.


00:44:54.182 --> 00:44:55.206
No.


00:44:57.885 --> 00:44:59.512
No.


00:44:59.988 --> 00:45:02.582
I'm not going
until I do what I've been trying to do...


00:45:02.757 --> 00:45:04.748
...since we first got here.


00:45:07.495 --> 00:45:12.194
Um, Velma, I learned something today.


00:45:12.367 --> 00:45:14.892
Life is like a chocolate soufflé.


00:45:15.603 --> 00:45:19.903
And if you wait too long to dig in,
it could just collapse on you.


00:45:20.575 --> 00:45:24.739
So anyway,
what I'm trying to say is...


00:45:29.284 --> 00:45:32.913
...Velma Dinkley,
will you go on a date with me?


00:45:34.022 --> 00:45:36.547
- Heh. A date?
- Yeah.


00:45:37.592 --> 00:45:39.423
Shaggy.


00:45:40.662 --> 00:45:42.323
Are you serious?


00:45:42.530 --> 00:45:46.330
I've never been more serious
about anything in my entire life.


00:45:46.567 --> 00:45:50.230
Except maybe dinosaurs,
but that was a long time ago.


00:45:51.439 --> 00:45:55.398
Shaggy, that's very sweet of you...


00:45:56.311 --> 00:45:59.838
...but we're right in the middle
of an investigation.


00:46:00.782 --> 00:46:03.808
Well, like,
I think Fred and Daphne can handle it.


00:46:04.052 --> 00:46:07.647
They probably wanna spend some
quality time together anyway, right?


00:46:07.822 --> 00:46:09.483
- No, not really.
- I'm good.


00:46:10.591 --> 00:46:12.957
I don't know, Shaggy.


00:46:13.127 --> 00:46:14.185
SHAGGY:
Oh.


00:46:15.596 --> 00:46:18.030
Like-- Like, yeah, that's--


00:46:18.199 --> 00:46:19.496
I mean, that's fine.


00:46:19.701 --> 00:46:21.066
I--


00:46:21.636 --> 00:46:24.298
If I were you, I probably
wouldn't wanna go on a date...


00:46:24.472 --> 00:46:26.770
...with a goofy guy
like me either so....


00:46:32.180 --> 00:46:34.080
Hold on.


00:46:34.782 --> 00:46:36.613
Shaggy, you know what?


00:46:37.318 --> 00:46:39.786
I will go on a date with you tonight.


00:46:40.355 --> 00:46:41.379
Oh, really?


00:46:42.824 --> 00:46:44.724
- You mean it?
- Sure.


00:46:44.892 --> 00:46:45.950
Why not?


00:46:46.160 --> 00:46:48.287
Yes.


00:46:48.830 --> 00:46:50.388
Pick you up around 7.


00:46:52.133 --> 00:46:53.600
[GRUNTS]


00:46:54.168 --> 00:46:55.226
Seven o'clock.


00:46:58.973 --> 00:47:00.463
Slippery.


00:47:01.342 --> 00:47:02.366
[PIANO CRASHES]


00:47:02.543 --> 00:47:04.135
- Ouch.
SHAGGY: I'm okay.


00:47:07.648 --> 00:47:09.809
Oh, curse this mop top.


00:47:09.984 --> 00:47:12.646
I can't do anything with it.


00:47:15.156 --> 00:47:17.590
Okay, Scoob, how do I look?


00:47:17.759 --> 00:47:19.920
Ah. Handsome as a devil.


00:47:20.128 --> 00:47:22.619
What about me?


00:47:23.030 --> 00:47:24.429
Oh. Um....


00:47:24.632 --> 00:47:26.657
Like, as dapper as a Dalmatian...


00:47:26.834 --> 00:47:31.362
- ...but where are you headed, buddy?
- With you. Where else?


00:47:31.572 --> 00:47:35.201
Oh, um, heh. Um....


00:47:35.410 --> 00:47:38.004
You know, buddy...


00:47:38.179 --> 00:47:41.910
...I'm gonna have to fly solo
on this one tonight.


00:47:42.083 --> 00:47:44.847
- Solo?
- Yeah, you know, like...


00:47:45.019 --> 00:47:48.352
...you're just gonna have to do
your own thing, you know what I mean?


00:47:48.523 --> 00:47:52.459
My own thing? But, Shaggy--


00:47:52.660 --> 00:47:55.788
Thanks for understanding, Scoob.


00:47:56.697 --> 00:47:58.028
[SIGHS]


00:47:58.199 --> 00:48:00.064
I'll see you later, pal.


00:48:00.234 --> 00:48:03.032
Goodbye, Shaggy.


00:48:03.204 --> 00:48:05.263
[CRYING]


00:48:16.184 --> 00:48:18.118
[SHAGGY WHIMPERING]


00:48:18.286 --> 00:48:21.744
Who's the best puppy
in the whole wide world?


00:48:23.291 --> 00:48:25.384
[CONTINUES WHIMPERING]


00:48:27.128 --> 00:48:31.064
No. No more rolling over.


00:48:44.512 --> 00:48:45.672
- Ready?
- Yeah.


00:48:45.847 --> 00:48:48.077
Good. So...


00:48:48.249 --> 00:48:49.841
...who were they?


00:48:50.017 --> 00:48:51.780
Who were who?


00:48:52.620 --> 00:48:53.678
Oh, ho.


00:48:53.855 --> 00:48:57.757
Are you still wondering about those boys
I was playing tennis with?


00:48:57.925 --> 00:49:00.621
They were nobody, Fred.
Just some caddies I met.


00:49:00.795 --> 00:49:02.262
Why?


00:49:02.763 --> 00:49:04.253
You're not jealous, are you?


00:49:04.432 --> 00:49:06.764
Jealous? No, no.


00:49:06.934 --> 00:49:08.765
I'm not jealous. No way.


00:49:08.936 --> 00:49:10.995
I don't get jealous.


00:49:11.172 --> 00:49:13.003
Yeah, right.


00:49:27.622 --> 00:49:29.055
[SNIFFING]


00:49:33.294 --> 00:49:35.854
- Good evening, Norville.
- Heh.


00:49:36.330 --> 00:49:37.797
[CHUCKLES]


00:49:38.466 --> 00:49:40.127
Shaggy.


00:49:41.002 --> 00:49:42.765
Aren't you gonna say anything?


00:49:46.007 --> 00:49:49.204
I like corn dogs.


00:49:56.307 --> 00:49:58.741
- Thanks, Shaggy.
- Yeah.


00:50:02.380 --> 00:50:03.938
Thank you.


00:50:04.816 --> 00:50:06.841
Oh. Ahem.


00:50:19.397 --> 00:50:20.625
[CLEARS THROAT]


00:50:22.734 --> 00:50:25.635
Well, it looks like we got
the whole place to ourselves.


00:50:25.870 --> 00:50:31.069
Yes, unfortunately, that only emphasizes
the urgency of our investigation.


00:50:31.276 --> 00:50:33.972
- Sure we shouldn't check with Fred--?
- Oh, come on, V.


00:50:34.145 --> 00:50:37.774
Like, just try to put those frontal lobes
on the back burner tonight, okay?


00:50:39.117 --> 00:50:40.880
Okay, Shaggy.


00:50:41.052 --> 00:50:44.954
I must admit, I do have a hard time
letting myself relax.


00:50:45.156 --> 00:50:47.124
Especially recently.


00:50:47.358 --> 00:50:50.987
Ever since we've been here,
I just haven't felt Iike myself.


00:50:53.498 --> 00:50:56.490
Well, whoever you are, I like it.


00:50:58.503 --> 00:50:59.731
Thanks, Shaggy.


00:51:02.006 --> 00:51:03.337
Oh. Um....


00:51:03.508 --> 00:51:07.774
Now, come on,
I want this night to be perfect.


00:51:08.613 --> 00:51:10.080
[SCREAMS]


00:51:11.182 --> 00:51:12.274
Velma.


00:51:13.618 --> 00:51:15.415
VELMA:
My glasses.


00:51:15.587 --> 00:51:16.918
Here, let me help you up.


00:51:17.088 --> 00:51:18.180
Are you okay?


00:51:18.389 --> 00:51:19.788
I'm sorry, I--


00:51:19.958 --> 00:51:22.586
I don't know what came over me.


00:51:23.294 --> 00:51:24.989
Oh, here. Here you go.


00:51:25.163 --> 00:51:26.425
- Thanks.
- Yeah.


00:51:30.168 --> 00:51:33.399
Oh, boy.
Here, let me get you some water.


00:51:33.605 --> 00:51:37.200
Garçon, water, please.


00:51:37.709 --> 00:51:39.768
[SPEAKING IN FRENCH]


00:51:39.978 --> 00:51:41.002
[LAUGHING]


00:51:41.980 --> 00:51:43.845
[HUMMING]


00:51:48.920 --> 00:51:49.944
[SCOOBY BELCHES]


00:51:50.121 --> 00:51:51.349
[SCOOBY SPEAKING IN FRENCH]


00:51:52.223 --> 00:51:55.715
Oh, whoops.
I seem to have dropped my fork.


00:51:56.494 --> 00:51:59.156
Here, help me find it, waiter.


00:52:00.365 --> 00:52:02.060
Scooby-Doo, what are you doing?


00:52:02.233 --> 00:52:05.361
Waiting tables. Fresh ground pepper?


00:52:05.536 --> 00:52:08.471
Scooby, get out of here, buddy.
You're gonna ruin everything.


00:52:08.640 --> 00:52:10.369
No.


00:52:10.875 --> 00:52:15.335
Okay, but would you do it
for a Scooby snack?


00:52:15.513 --> 00:52:18.346
I can't be bought. Hmph.


00:52:19.217 --> 00:52:20.411
Now, you listen, Scoob...


00:52:20.585 --> 00:52:23.577
...I'm the master and I command you
to go back to your room...


00:52:23.755 --> 00:52:26.849
...and quit being such a bad dog.


00:52:28.760 --> 00:52:30.193
Puppy loving....


00:52:30.395 --> 00:52:32.488
[SCOOBY MUTTERING INDISTINCTLY]


00:52:33.498 --> 00:52:35.363
Bad dog? Huh.


00:52:35.566 --> 00:52:37.864
I'll show you a bad dog.


00:52:38.169 --> 00:52:40.364
[LAUGHS THEN GROWLS]


00:52:40.772 --> 00:52:42.831
No, Shaggy, don't.
The waiter will bring--


00:52:43.007 --> 00:52:44.338
[SCREAMS]


00:52:45.677 --> 00:52:47.406
Would you care to hear our specials?


00:52:47.578 --> 00:52:49.739
Scooby-Doo? Is that you?


00:52:49.981 --> 00:52:51.778
I didn't invite him.


00:52:52.016 --> 00:52:55.179
He just showed up
and tried to sabotage everything and--


00:52:55.353 --> 00:52:57.685
- And--
- Is that what I think it is?


00:52:59.991 --> 00:53:01.219
Oh, uh, heh.


00:53:01.392 --> 00:53:04.884
Yeah, that was supposed to be
a surprise.


00:53:05.096 --> 00:53:07.257
I found it in a sand trap last night.


00:53:07.498 --> 00:53:10.228
It's one of those moonstones, right?


00:53:10.802 --> 00:53:11.860
Yes.


00:53:12.070 --> 00:53:16.063
I was gonna give it to you when I walked
you back to your room tonight, but....


00:53:16.240 --> 00:53:18.401
It's beautiful.


00:53:20.545 --> 00:53:23.139
Excuse me, I have to go now.


00:53:23.815 --> 00:53:26.909
Wait, what? Well, Velma--


00:53:29.520 --> 00:53:31.317
This is all your fault, Scooby-Doo.


00:53:31.522 --> 00:53:33.387
You ruined everything.


00:53:33.558 --> 00:53:36.152
No, I didn't.


00:53:36.327 --> 00:53:37.794
[SCOOBY GROWLS]


00:53:47.105 --> 00:53:49.733
DAPHNE:
There it is, the purple boat.


00:53:49.907 --> 00:53:52.068
FRED:
She. There she is.


00:53:52.276 --> 00:53:53.675
A boat is a she, like a girl.


00:53:53.845 --> 00:53:56.006
But not one who goes around
playing tennis...


00:53:56.180 --> 00:53:58.648
...with every boy boat in the harbor.


00:54:08.693 --> 00:54:11.093
That cloaked figure
was definitely here.


00:54:11.262 --> 00:54:13.423
All hands on deck.


00:54:35.286 --> 00:54:37.948
Fred, look.


00:54:48.699 --> 00:54:50.826
- Ladies first.
- Mm-mm.


00:54:51.002 --> 00:54:52.492
Fine.


00:55:34.946 --> 00:55:37.506
Looks like a bunch of old newspapers.


00:55:37.682 --> 00:55:38.910
DAPHNE:
I'll say.


00:55:39.183 --> 00:55:40.650
FRED:
Huh.


00:55:41.953 --> 00:55:46.890
Hey, these are about that witch
from Uggins' story, Wanda Grubwort.


00:55:47.058 --> 00:55:49.959
DAPHNE: Evil staff?
- Yeah, remember? Didn't Elmer say...


00:55:50.161 --> 00:55:53.153
...an ancient staff was the source
of her black magic?


00:55:55.299 --> 00:55:56.960
DAPHNE:
Hey, look at this one.


00:55:59.036 --> 00:56:03.302
That must be what the monster's doing,
looking for the source of her powers.


00:56:03.474 --> 00:56:06.705
The problem is we still don't know
who's controlling it.


00:56:07.678 --> 00:56:10.374
Wait a second, maybe we do.


00:56:12.416 --> 00:56:16.113
Wanda Grubwort had children. She could
still have descendants living in town.


00:56:16.287 --> 00:56:17.549
Maybe one got angry...


00:56:17.722 --> 00:56:20.885
...when your uncle built on their land
and decided to get revenge.


00:56:23.628 --> 00:56:25.425
What was that?


00:56:28.199 --> 00:56:30.497
It's locked. Hello!


00:56:30.735 --> 00:56:32.430
Help. Help.


00:56:32.603 --> 00:56:36.198
DAPHNE:
Anyone out there? Let us out.


00:56:38.609 --> 00:56:39.667
Help. Help.


00:56:39.844 --> 00:56:42.142
Is anyone out there? Oh, great.


00:56:42.313 --> 00:56:44.645
If we don't get this open,
we'll be stuck here all night.


00:56:44.815 --> 00:56:46.305
[RUMBLING]


00:56:47.418 --> 00:56:49.249
That might be the least
of our worries.


00:56:50.154 --> 00:56:51.519
- Hello!
- Is anyone out there?


00:56:51.722 --> 00:56:52.746
Help!


00:56:53.624 --> 00:56:55.922
- Help, help!
DAPHNE: We need to get out.


00:56:56.093 --> 00:56:57.788
FRED: Help, anybody.
DAPHNE: Anyone!


00:56:57.995 --> 00:57:00.793
FRED: Help, anybody!
- Help, get us out!


00:57:00.965 --> 00:57:03.263
FRED:
Help, help, anybody!


00:57:03.467 --> 00:57:06.925
- Help, help.
- We're stuck, it's filling.


00:57:07.772 --> 00:57:10.468
Fred, you need to do something.
We're gonna drown.


00:57:10.675 --> 00:57:14.634
I have an idea. Why don't we call
those guys you were playing tennis with?


00:57:14.812 --> 00:57:18.543
- I knew it, you are jealous.
- Yeah, maybe I am.


00:57:18.749 --> 00:57:22.116
- Good, that was the point.
- You were just lying to make me jealous?


00:57:22.286 --> 00:57:25.722
Yes, I'm trying to pay you back
for playing golf with those floozies.


00:57:25.890 --> 00:57:28.120
Flooz--? Oh, that was different.


00:57:28.292 --> 00:57:30.317
How? How was that any different?


00:57:30.494 --> 00:57:32.826
I don't know, they were-- It just was.


00:57:32.997 --> 00:57:34.658
All right, you know what, Fred?


00:57:34.832 --> 00:57:38.165
If I'm gonna die,
I don't want to die dating a jerk.


00:57:38.336 --> 00:57:41.999
Yeah, well, if I'm gonna die,
I don't want to die dating a sneaky...


00:57:42.673 --> 00:57:45.506
...manipulative, game-playing....


00:57:51.048 --> 00:57:53.482
You see that? I saved us.


00:57:53.651 --> 00:57:57.087
That's Iovely,
but we're still broken up.


00:57:57.288 --> 00:57:58.312
What?


00:57:58.522 --> 00:58:00.217
Good.


00:58:00.925 --> 00:58:03.018
[MUTTERING]


00:58:26.083 --> 00:58:27.880
Like, what happened to you guys?


00:58:28.085 --> 00:58:29.416
What happened?


00:58:29.587 --> 00:58:31.248
We broke up, that's what happened.


00:58:31.455 --> 00:58:33.685
Yeah, best decision I ever made too.


00:58:33.891 --> 00:58:36.382
Did you just say best decision
you ever made?


00:58:36.560 --> 00:58:39.085
That's funny,
because I broke up with you.


00:58:39.263 --> 00:58:40.287
[BOTH CHUCKLE]


00:58:40.464 --> 00:58:42.193
What? You did not.


00:58:42.366 --> 00:58:44.061
- Guys?
DAPHNE: I did so.


00:58:44.235 --> 00:58:45.896
Guys.


00:58:46.103 --> 00:58:51.439
That's a real bummer and all,
but I kind of meant, why are you wet?


00:58:51.776 --> 00:58:53.266
Oh, that.


00:58:53.444 --> 00:58:56.436
Well, let's just say we almost got in
over our heads.


00:58:56.614 --> 00:58:59.708
But we figured out
that Wanda Grubwort's descendant...


00:58:59.884 --> 00:59:03.650
...might be trying to reconstruct
her magical staff.


00:59:06.624 --> 00:59:10.219
Hey, how'd it go with Velma?


00:59:11.595 --> 00:59:14.894
Yeah. Ask my waiter.


00:59:15.099 --> 00:59:17.465
DAPHNE:
Grubek, Grubel, Guzzak.


00:59:18.269 --> 00:59:19.293
No Grubwort.


00:59:19.970 --> 00:59:24.771
Huh. Would you look at that.
What a crazy coincidence.


00:59:25.810 --> 00:59:27.869
What's that, Shags?


00:59:28.312 --> 00:59:32.408
Oh. Remember that creepy general store
we stopped at on the way in?


00:59:32.950 --> 00:59:35.077
It was called Trowburgs.


00:59:35.252 --> 00:59:39.780
Well, if you spell Trowburg backwards
you get Grubwort.


00:59:39.990 --> 00:59:41.321
What are the odds, huh?


00:59:41.492 --> 00:59:45.019
Excuse me,
you are on my side of the room.


00:59:54.839 --> 00:59:56.306
[SHAGGY & SCOOBY GULP]


01:00:09.186 --> 01:00:10.483
[THUNDER CRASHING]


01:00:12.289 --> 01:00:14.223
There. Shaggy, Scooby,
go around back.


01:00:14.425 --> 01:00:16.723
- I'm not going with him.
- I'm not going with him.


01:00:16.927 --> 01:00:19.259
- You think I want to go with you?
SHAGGY: Seriously--


01:00:19.430 --> 01:00:21.295
SCOOBY: I'm not going with Shaggy.
FRED: Enough.


01:00:21.465 --> 01:00:23.626
- Guys, let's just go.
- Go.


01:00:27.638 --> 01:00:29.367
- Surprise.
WOMAN: Oh, no.


01:00:29.540 --> 01:00:30.973
[WOMAN CACKLING]


01:00:31.142 --> 01:00:32.803
Come on.


01:00:33.511 --> 01:00:34.978
Hey, wait for me.


01:00:45.156 --> 01:00:46.851
In here.


01:00:54.899 --> 01:00:56.696
SCOOBY:
This way.


01:00:57.468 --> 01:00:59.095
The other way.


01:01:04.208 --> 01:01:05.675
[SHAGGY SCREAMING]


01:01:08.846 --> 01:01:09.870
No.


01:01:11.615 --> 01:01:14.243
FRED: Come on.
SHAGGY: No, please.


01:01:14.418 --> 01:01:15.976
Please.


01:01:22.726 --> 01:01:24.887
- Now can we split up?
- Ugh.


01:01:29.934 --> 01:01:32.528
SHAGGY: Hey, come on, Scoob.
- I'm right behind you, Shaggy.


01:01:32.703 --> 01:01:34.762
[SHAGGY SCREAMS]


01:01:35.306 --> 01:01:37.536
Change of plans.


01:01:41.011 --> 01:01:43.912
WOMAN:
And stay out.


01:01:46.717 --> 01:01:49.880
Time to unmask
the person behind this mystery.


01:01:51.589 --> 01:01:54.285
- It's you?
- What?


01:01:54.458 --> 01:01:56.653
Like, it can't be.


01:01:59.029 --> 01:02:00.257
Velma?


01:02:01.232 --> 01:02:04.565
[IN DISTORTED VOICE]
Oh, you fools. I'm not Velma.


01:02:05.603 --> 01:02:07.002
[DAPHNE SCREAMS]


01:02:07.171 --> 01:02:09.071
Daphne.


01:02:10.574 --> 01:02:12.633
I don't want to hurt you, Velma.


01:02:12.843 --> 01:02:15.539
Oh, but I do want to hurt you,
pretty boy.


01:02:17.081 --> 01:02:18.571
Sorry, Velma.


01:02:18.749 --> 01:02:20.944
[GRUNTING]


01:02:26.190 --> 01:02:29.990
Velma. What's going on?
Why are you doing this?


01:02:30.194 --> 01:02:31.957
Our date wasn't that bad, was it?


01:02:32.162 --> 01:02:37.623
Why? To make them pay,
to make them all pay.


01:02:37.801 --> 01:02:42.761
Now, that I've rebuilt my staff,
no one can stop me.


01:02:50.881 --> 01:02:52.348
[COUGHING]


01:03:00.724 --> 01:03:05.627
Well, there's another mystery solved,
huh, gang?


01:03:06.196 --> 01:03:07.493
I got it.


01:03:07.665 --> 01:03:09.326
Okay.


01:03:10.601 --> 01:03:14.799
What in the world is going on?
Why is Velma doing this?


01:03:15.306 --> 01:03:16.603
Oh, no.


01:03:16.807 --> 01:03:19.674
You don't think my passions
drove her mad, do you?


01:03:19.843 --> 01:03:22.334
I'm sure there's something bigger
than that going on.


01:03:22.513 --> 01:03:23.810
I'll say.


01:03:24.848 --> 01:03:29.547
Your friend has been possessed by
the spirit of the witch Wanda Grubwort.


01:03:30.220 --> 01:03:34.987
Oh, great, my first love
and she's turned into an evil witch.


01:03:35.159 --> 01:03:37.218
Join the club.


01:03:45.669 --> 01:03:48.194
Yeah. Hee, hee, hee.


01:03:48.372 --> 01:03:49.532
It was that staff.


01:03:49.707 --> 01:03:51.072
[IMITATES EXPLOSION]


01:03:51.241 --> 01:03:53.607
She must have found the pieces...


01:03:53.777 --> 01:03:57.577
...that have been buried
all these many years.


01:03:58.215 --> 01:04:00.740
Like, by any chance...


01:04:00.918 --> 01:04:03.682
...did moonstones
play any part in this?


01:04:04.254 --> 01:04:07.917
As soon as your friend touched one
of those rocks...


01:04:08.092 --> 01:04:11.459
...the spirit of my evil ancestor
took hold of her...


01:04:11.662 --> 01:04:15.063
...and compelled her to find the rest.


01:04:15.232 --> 01:04:17.792
SCOOBY: For you, old lady.
- Oh.


01:04:19.069 --> 01:04:22.527
So it's been Velma the entire time?


01:04:22.740 --> 01:04:26.540
Like, zoinks.
It's been right under our noses.


01:04:26.744 --> 01:04:29.235
The evil spirit must have first taken
hold of her...


01:04:29.413 --> 01:04:31.472
...when we found that stone
by the lake.


01:04:32.282 --> 01:04:36.480
And those creepy warts, it was like
she was actually turning into a witch.


01:04:36.720 --> 01:04:38.119
Being burned at the stake...


01:04:38.288 --> 01:04:41.223
...would make me pretty freaked out
at the sight of fire too.


01:04:41.425 --> 01:04:44.417
And I bet she intentionally shorted out
the security console...


01:04:44.595 --> 01:04:46.995
...because she knew
we'd see her face.


01:04:47.598 --> 01:04:49.623
I can't believe we missed it.


01:04:49.800 --> 01:04:52.792
I guess we were all too wrapped up
in our own little dramas...


01:04:52.970 --> 01:04:55.438
...to catch the really big one going on.


01:04:56.273 --> 01:04:57.297
[SIGHS]


01:04:57.808 --> 01:05:03.246
So now that she has her powers back,
what's Wanda Grubwort going to do?


01:05:03.414 --> 01:05:06.850
I fear that what she seeks
is the revenge...


01:05:07.017 --> 01:05:10.453
...that has eluded her all these years.


01:05:11.221 --> 01:05:13.018
Who cares about what she wants.


01:05:13.223 --> 01:05:17.250
We gotta save Velma. Do you have
any idea where she would have gone?


01:05:17.461 --> 01:05:20.157
Oh, probably to the caves
where she lived.


01:05:20.330 --> 01:05:21.592
The caves?


01:05:21.799 --> 01:05:24.495
But what about the irrigated
rudimentary claymations?


01:05:24.735 --> 01:05:25.759
The what?


01:05:25.936 --> 01:05:29.099
The entrances to the caves,
they're all underwater.


01:05:29.273 --> 01:05:30.638
How would we get in?


01:05:31.608 --> 01:05:34.008
You're in luck. I rent scuba gear.


01:05:34.244 --> 01:05:36.940
I'll give you a good deal too.


01:05:49.493 --> 01:05:51.484
Smile.


01:06:34.204 --> 01:06:36.399
Zoinks.


01:06:49.019 --> 01:06:50.884
FRED:
Lights.


01:07:09.706 --> 01:07:10.730
Uh-oh.


01:07:18.448 --> 01:07:20.109
VELMA [IN DISTORTED VOICE]:
Ah.


01:07:20.284 --> 01:07:23.310
You've been a faithful servant.


01:07:23.487 --> 01:07:28.447
And now I think you deserve
some playmates.


01:07:28.625 --> 01:07:30.252
[BELLOWS]


01:07:32.362 --> 01:07:34.455
She's making more of those things.


01:07:41.672 --> 01:07:44.163
VELMA:
Rise, my slithering slaves.


01:07:44.408 --> 01:07:47.900
Rise and serve your new master.


01:07:52.983 --> 01:07:55.076
[GROWLING]


01:07:55.452 --> 01:07:56.476
[GASPS]


01:07:56.653 --> 01:07:58.951
Finally, we'll make them pay.


01:07:59.122 --> 01:08:02.614
Make them rue the day
they set foot on our land.


01:08:03.293 --> 01:08:05.818
Those things are gonna attack
everyone in town.


01:08:05.996 --> 01:08:09.124
- We have to do something.
- What can we do?


01:08:09.299 --> 01:08:12.928
Hey, Fred, I know this is usually
your department, but do you mind--?


01:08:13.103 --> 01:08:15.970
- If you've got a plan, Shaggy, go for it.
- Okay.


01:08:17.307 --> 01:08:21.004
Velma Dacey Dinkley,
you stop that this instant.


01:08:22.112 --> 01:08:27.948
I told you,
Velma doesn't live here anymore.


01:08:28.151 --> 01:08:30.619
That was your big idea, Shags?


01:08:30.821 --> 01:08:34.154
Creatures, change of plans.


01:08:34.358 --> 01:08:35.620
Get them.


01:08:36.960 --> 01:08:38.951
SCOOBY:
Hold still.


01:08:42.366 --> 01:08:43.993
Thank you. Aah!


01:08:55.245 --> 01:08:56.303
Velma.


01:08:56.480 --> 01:09:00.211
Velma, I know you're still in there.
I know you can hear me.


01:09:02.219 --> 01:09:05.154
Okay, like, maybe you can't.


01:09:09.793 --> 01:09:11.226
DAPHNE:
This is like biology class...


01:09:11.395 --> 01:09:14.558
...except this time
the frogs are gonna dissect us.


01:09:16.500 --> 01:09:18.730
Like, come on, V.
You gotta listen to me.


01:09:18.902 --> 01:09:21.769
You're stronger than this thing
inside of you.


01:09:22.005 --> 01:09:26.374
You're stronger
and you're smarter and you're cuter.


01:09:27.244 --> 01:09:30.008
- [IN NORMAL VOICE] I am?
- That's right, V.


01:09:30.180 --> 01:09:33.843
I think everything about you is cute.
Like the way...


01:09:34.017 --> 01:09:36.747
...your pleated skirt ruffles
when you run from ghosts.


01:09:36.987 --> 01:09:38.352
How-- And even--


01:09:38.522 --> 01:09:42.686
Even how you lose your glasses
at the most inopportune moments.


01:09:42.859 --> 01:09:48.058
Yeah. Yeah, as a matter of fact,
that might be the cutest thing of all.


01:09:48.999 --> 01:09:50.899
Shaggy?


01:09:51.568 --> 01:09:53.934
- Help me.
- Yeah.


01:09:54.137 --> 01:09:57.197
Yeah, listen, V.
You gotta fight this old witch.


01:09:57.407 --> 01:09:58.431
- Okay.
- Okay?


01:09:58.608 --> 01:10:01.543
Shaggy, I'll try. I'll try.


01:10:01.712 --> 01:10:03.577
[IN DISTORTED VOICE]
No, you won't.


01:10:04.715 --> 01:10:06.546
[SHAGGY SCREAMING]


01:10:10.754 --> 01:10:15.384
Well, at least now I can finally say
I've been picked up by a girl.


01:10:36.913 --> 01:10:39.177
See you, froggies.


01:10:47.991 --> 01:10:50.152
FRED:
Run, run.


01:10:59.836 --> 01:11:02.304
That ought to hold them for a while.
Come on.


01:11:07.477 --> 01:11:09.945
Knock me down all you want,
Wanda Grubwort...


01:11:10.147 --> 01:11:14.709
...but I'm not gonna let a couple of
stupid moonstones take my friend away.


01:11:15.719 --> 01:11:18.085
Oh, wait, moon. Oh, that's it.


01:11:19.022 --> 01:11:22.185
[SINGING]
By the light of the silvery moon


01:11:22.359 --> 01:11:23.519
What is it? What are you--?


01:11:23.693 --> 01:11:25.558
By the light


01:11:25.729 --> 01:11:27.458
[IN NORMAL VOICE]
Not the dark but the light


01:11:28.665 --> 01:11:31.031
Of the silvery moon


01:11:31.201 --> 01:11:33.829
Not the sun, but the moon


01:11:34.004 --> 01:11:35.995
I want to spoon


01:11:36.173 --> 01:11:37.731
[IN DISTORTED VOICE]
No, you're mine.


01:11:37.974 --> 01:11:42.377
- To my honey I'll croon love's tune
- [IN NORMAL VOICE] Croon love's tune


01:11:43.013 --> 01:11:47.882
- Oh, by the light of the silvery
- Light of the silvery


01:11:48.385 --> 01:11:50.876
VELMA: Moon
WANDA: Oh!


01:11:51.054 --> 01:11:52.646
[GROANING]


01:12:00.363 --> 01:12:01.489
It's a dead end.


01:12:05.168 --> 01:12:07.193
I'm sorry, Daph.


01:12:07.370 --> 01:12:08.928
I really was a jerk.


01:12:09.172 --> 01:12:10.935
I'm sorry too, Fred.


01:12:11.141 --> 01:12:14.167
I never should've tried
to make you jealous.


01:12:15.078 --> 01:12:17.273
[MONSTERS ROARING]


01:12:18.782 --> 01:12:23.719
Get out of me, Wanda Grubwort.


01:12:26.756 --> 01:12:28.849
[WANDA SCREAMING]


01:12:33.263 --> 01:12:37.757
Nothing can stop me now. Come.


01:12:53.116 --> 01:12:55.084
SCOOBY:
Not so fast.


01:12:55.285 --> 01:12:57.048
What? No.


01:12:57.621 --> 01:13:00.920
Say goodbye, wicked witch.


01:13:01.124 --> 01:13:06.152
No, no. Revenge was in my grasp.


01:13:06.329 --> 01:13:08.729
And I would have gotten away
with it...


01:13:08.899 --> 01:13:13.734
...if it wasn't for you meddling kids
and your rotten dog.


01:13:13.904 --> 01:13:14.928
[GIGGLES]


01:13:15.105 --> 01:13:19.201
Oh, no. No.


01:13:20.243 --> 01:13:22.108
[SCREAMS]


01:13:23.013 --> 01:13:25.106
[MONSTERS SLITHERING]


01:13:30.820 --> 01:13:32.287
[FROGS CROAKING]


01:13:36.092 --> 01:13:38.583
Shaggy did it. Come on.


01:13:40.297 --> 01:13:42.128
VELMA:
Shaggy?


01:13:43.500 --> 01:13:45.365
Is it over?


01:13:49.472 --> 01:13:51.838
I think so, V.


01:13:54.010 --> 01:13:56.171
Those things you said to me.


01:13:58.114 --> 01:13:59.775
Did you really mean all of that?


01:14:00.884 --> 01:14:02.943
Of course I did.


01:14:03.153 --> 01:14:06.486
I've been trying to say it
ever since we got here.


01:14:09.125 --> 01:14:11.252
Just kiss her already.


01:14:11.761 --> 01:14:14.025
Oh, well, I--


01:14:14.264 --> 01:14:16.789
Shaggy, just kiss me already.


01:14:27.277 --> 01:14:28.744
SHAGGY:
Well, um....


01:14:28.912 --> 01:14:30.539
That was, uh....


01:14:31.381 --> 01:14:32.780
Yeah.


01:14:33.817 --> 01:14:37.150
You know,
I don't know too much about chemistry.


01:14:37.320 --> 01:14:39.220
I do, Shaggy.


01:14:39.422 --> 01:14:44.826
And, well, there just wasn't any.


01:14:44.995 --> 01:14:47.020
Yeah, I....


01:14:47.831 --> 01:14:52.165
You know, maybe we're just better off
being friends.


01:14:52.335 --> 01:14:54.895
You know what? Maybe we all are.


01:14:55.071 --> 01:14:56.561
Yeah.


01:14:57.574 --> 01:14:58.871
Phew.


01:14:59.042 --> 01:15:02.705
THORNY: Well, kids, with the creature
gone, we have a ton of new applications.


01:15:02.879 --> 01:15:04.608
Maybe more than we can handle.


01:15:05.248 --> 01:15:07.842
- And it's all thanks to you guys.
- Aw.


01:15:10.520 --> 01:15:13.250
Oh, that reminds me.


01:15:15.859 --> 01:15:20.353
FRED: What?
- Something to show my appreciation.


01:15:20.530 --> 01:15:23.397
- Ten thousand dollars?
- Uncle Thorny.


01:15:23.566 --> 01:15:25.193
- Oh.
- Aw.


01:15:27.470 --> 01:15:31.099
By the way, I took the liberty to set up
an appointment with my attorney...


01:15:31.274 --> 01:15:33.037
...for you to discuss incorporating.


01:15:33.710 --> 01:15:36.543
Thought that might help
with your future liability issues.


01:15:36.713 --> 01:15:38.112
- Yeah.
- Oh, man.


01:15:38.281 --> 01:15:41.148
- Shall we go play around?
SHAGGY: This is gonna be amazing, guys.


01:15:41.351 --> 01:15:43.876
- So insane.
- Hey, you guys, I've got it.


01:15:44.054 --> 01:15:46.284
We can be Mystery Incorporated.


01:15:46.456 --> 01:15:48.481
- I love it.
- I can totally dig that.


01:15:48.658 --> 01:15:50.057
Hey, Scooby, get a picture.


01:15:50.260 --> 01:15:51.591
[LAUGHS]


01:15:51.761 --> 01:15:53.160
FRED:
Everybody say, "Mystery Inc."


01:15:53.396 --> 01:15:55.796
ALL:
Mystery Inc.


01:15:55.965 --> 01:15:58.058
- Oh, my goodness.
- Guys, group hug.


01:15:58.234 --> 01:16:00.099
- Okay.
- Okay, all right.


01:16:00.270 --> 01:16:02.101
VELMA: Okay, Shaggy.
DAPHNE: Shaggy.


01:16:02.272 --> 01:16:04.638
VELMA: Shaggy.
FRED: Okay....


01:16:05.975 --> 01:16:08.307
All right. We'll celebrate.


01:16:08.511 --> 01:16:09.569
All right. Bye, guys.


01:16:09.746 --> 01:16:12.146
Not the hair, man. Not the hair.


01:16:13.316 --> 01:16:14.442
[SIGHS]


01:16:15.652 --> 01:16:17.313
[WHIMPERING]


01:16:17.487 --> 01:16:19.580
[GRUNTING]


01:16:33.269 --> 01:16:34.293
Don't worry, Scoob.


01:16:35.004 --> 01:16:38.838
No matter what happens,
I'll always be here for you.


01:16:39.042 --> 01:16:41.636
Oh, Shaggy.


01:16:54.290 --> 01:16:56.383
[SINGING]
When danger used to come around


01:16:56.559 --> 01:16:58.618
I would fall right to the ground


01:16:58.795 --> 01:17:01.025
It's true


01:17:03.166 --> 01:17:06.192
But now that I can see your face


01:17:06.369 --> 01:17:11.238
Well, I can stand up to anything


01:17:11.441 --> 01:17:14.205
And how I cherish the times


01:17:14.377 --> 01:17:19.144
When the sun shines on the two of us


01:17:19.549 --> 01:17:21.016
But I don't mind going through


01:17:21.184 --> 01:17:26.520
The bad times
Just as long as they're with you


01:17:27.090 --> 01:17:30.526
Well, I can be scared with you


01:17:31.661 --> 01:17:34.027
I can be alone with you


01:17:35.465 --> 01:17:39.731
As long as I have your hand
To hold onto


01:17:39.903 --> 01:17:45.239
I can be scared with you


01:17:45.408 --> 01:17:48.070
[CHORUS HUMMING]


01:17:51.247 --> 01:17:55.115
I can be scared with you


01:17:55.285 --> 01:18:00.780
Oh, I can be scared
As long as I'm with you


01:18:03.593 --> 01:18:07.620
I can do anything


01:18:07.797 --> 01:18:10.925
I can do anything


01:18:11.100 --> 01:18:16.902
As long as I'm with you


01:18:17.307 --> 01:18:19.400
[DISCO MUSIC PLAYING]


01:18:32.088 --> 01:18:34.522
[SINGING]
I can be scared with you


01:18:36.226 --> 01:18:38.558
I can be alone with you


01:18:40.063 --> 01:18:42.554
I can be scared with you


01:18:43.733 --> 01:18:46.566
As long as I'm with you


01:18:48.271 --> 01:18:50.296
My name is Shaggy
I like to eat


01:18:50.540 --> 01:18:52.167
Main man Scooby
But he got four feet


01:18:52.408 --> 01:18:55.400
Me and my homeys solve mysteries
Through cartoons, movies


01:18:55.578 --> 01:18:56.602
And tons of DVDs


01:18:56.779 --> 01:19:00.340
As old school goes, we're genuine
We've been kicking it since 1969


01:19:00.583 --> 01:19:02.448
But Mystery Inc. is far from through


01:19:02.619 --> 01:19:05.611
Because there's always more adventures
Starring me Scooby-Doo


01:19:23.573 --> 01:19:26.633
Scooby-Dooby-Doo.



